    "manual.more.title9": "Right-click menu",
    "manual.notify.desc1": `To the new **owner**. If the start time hasn't arrived yet, it's held until then and sent at the start time as "A new task has been assigned".`,
    "manual.notify.desc10": "Only to **recipients who haven't confirmed** yet. People who already confirmed don't receive it. Sent even before the start time.",
    "manual.notify.desc11": "For started tasks, to the **author + owner + CCs**; for tasks not yet started, only to the **author**. The person who marked it done is excluded.",
    "manual.notify.desc12": 'Checking a to-do sends "A to-do was completed" to everyone involved for started tasks, or to the author if not yet started. Unchecking · reordering sends nothing.',
    "manual.notify.desc13": "Goes to no one — it isn't an approval, it just clears the indicator on the author's screen.",
    "manual.notify.desc14": "To the **person who marked it done** (usually the owner). The reason is included and also left as a comment.",
    "manual.notify.desc15": "To the **owner + author**, at the time chosen for each task (e.g. 1 day before).",
    "manual.notify.desc16": "To the **owner + author**.",
    "manual.notify.desc17": "To the **owner + author**, for tasks past their due date that aren't done.",
    "manual.notify.desc18": "Whoever writes, to **everyone involved + the previous commenter** (except the commenter).",
    "manual.notify.desc19": "To the **author + previous commenter**. Comments by the author go to the **previous commenter + CCs** (the owner receives nothing until the start time).",
    "manual.notify.desc2": 'Besides the new owner, the **author and previous owner** also get "Owner changed". No assignment notification if you take it yourself (Take) or the author is the owner.',
    "manual.notify.desc20": "To the **person mentioned**. Can't be turned off.",
    "manual.notify.desc21": "Only to the **person who wrote the comment**.",
    "manual.notify.desc22": "To the **notice author + previous commenter** — recipients may be all employees, so it isn't sent to every recipient.",
    "manual.notify.desc23": "To the **owner + author** (except the editor; the owner from the start time). CCs are excluded.",
    "manual.notify.desc24": "To the **author + recipients**. For notices not yet posted (scheduled), only the author receives it.",
    "manual.notify.desc25": "Editing several fields in a row is bundled into one, with a summary of what changed and how.",
    "manual.notify.desc26": "Completion · archiving · sort order · owner/CC changes — each has its own notification, so they don't count as edits. To-do changes on already completed tasks aren't notified either.",
    "manual.notify.desc27": "Goes to the **owner · CCs** of started tasks and the **attendees** of events. Deleting · restoring · permanently deleting notices isn't notified.",
    "manual.notify.desc28": "To **all recipients** (all employees or the selected people). If the post time is set in the future, it's sent at that time.",
    "manual.notify.desc29": "Only to newly added **recipients**.",
    "manual.notify.desc3": "Only to the **author** (not CCs).",
    "manual.notify.desc30": "Goes to no one. The author sees the confirmation status (n/m).",
    "manual.notify.desc31": "You aren't notified about things you did yourself — if you completed it, you don't get the completion notification.",
    "manual.notify.desc32": "For tasks whose start time hasn't arrived, the owner gets no assignment · edit · comment · completion · due notifications, not even in the bell. For tasks with a future start time, CCs don't receive them either. Review requests · events · notices are exceptions.",
    "manual.notify.desc33": "Turn them off in profile menu › **Settings** › **Task notification types** (owner assignment · owner change · CC · event invitation · comments · comment reactions · confirmations · completion · rejection · task edits · due · overdue). Types you turn off come through neither the bell nor push.",
    "manual.notify.desc34": "Review requests · @mentions · notice posts · deletions · document requests · submissions · bug reports and handling · task transfers · automation rule notifications always come.",
    "manual.notify.desc35": "Turning off the task box under **Notification settings** in the same **Settings** window stops only app push; the bell list still fills up.",
    "manual.notify.desc36": "Tasks in the sample workspace don't send notifications.",
    "manual.notify.desc37": "Task box notifications are only the bell and app push — they aren't sent by text message or KakaoTalk.",
    "manual.notify.desc4": "Only to newly added **CCs**. Existing CCs don't receive it. If the start time is in the future, it's held until then.",
    "manual.notify.desc5": "Held assignment · CC notifications go out together at this time. Creation notifications for scheduled notices also go out at the post time.",
    "manual.notify.desc6": "To the event's **attendees**.",
    "manual.notify.desc7": `One message to the **recipient**: "You received N tasks from ○○" (with the note). If an admin transferred on someone's behalf, the original owner gets it too. When the recipient presses **Received**, the person who transferred is notified.`,
    "manual.notify.desc8": "To the **author**. A signal that the recipient has read it.",
    "manual.notify.desc9": "Goes to no one — there can be many CCs, so notifications would pour in per person. Visible only in the confirmation status (n/m).",
    "manual.notify.intro1": `Notifications go two ways: the bell (notification list) and app push. If someone isn't listed under "recipients" below, they get no notification when that happens. Many rules split on the **start time** — tasks that haven't started yet leave the owner undisturbed.`,
    "manual.notify.lead1": "All due-related notifications go only to the owner and author. CCs don't receive due notifications — sending them to CCs would turn notifications into noise. Tasks before their start time don't send due notifications either.",
    "manual.notify.lead2": "Everyone involved receives comments on started tasks. For tasks not yet started, only people directly in the conversation receive them.",
    "manual.notify.lead3": "Edit notifications aren't sent on every edit; they're bundled into one when the detail view is closed (**Save** on mobile) — so multiple notifications aren't sent while you're still editing.",
    "manual.notify.tabTitle1": "Notifications",
    "manual.notify.term1": "Assigned as owner",
    "manual.notify.term10": "Review request (reminder)",
