    "manual.notify.title1": "When tasks are assigned and received",
    "manual.notify.title2": "Confirm · Done · Review",
    "manual.notify.title3": "Due dates",
    "manual.notify.title4": "Comments · Reactions",
    "manual.notify.title5": "When content changes",
    "manual.notify.title6": "Notices",
    "manual.notify.title7": "Good to know",
    "manual.roles.desc1": "Write what needs doing by when and send it to the owner. Once it's done, review the result and clear it with **Review done**, or write a reason and **revert** it if it falls short.",
    "manual.roles.desc10": "If you change the owner to someone else (right-click › **Change owner**), you stay on as a CC. To hand over several tasks with a note, use **Task transfer** (More tab).",
    "manual.roles.desc11": "There is one owner. Work shared by several people is split into to-dos or created as separate tasks.",
    "manual.roles.desc12": "Read the content and comment if needed. Record that you've read it with the **Confirm** button.",
    "manual.roles.desc13": "Included in confirmation. A CC's confirmation doesn't send a notification and only updates the confirmation status (n/m) — with many people, notifications would get noisy.",
    "manual.roles.desc14": `Can edit as an involved person. However, if the workspace's **edit permission** is "Owner · author only", CCs and owners can't edit (including completion).`,
    "manual.roles.desc15": "Can't. Completion belongs to the author and owner.",
    "manual.roles.desc16": "Not received — due-related notifications go only to the owner and author (sending them to CCs would be noise).",
    "manual.roles.desc17": 'Everyone involved. People who can see the task without being involved can edit to-dos and attachments. If the workspace is set to "Owner · author only", only those two can; in a view-only workspace, no one can edit anything.',
    "manual.roles.desc18": "Author · owner.",
    "manual.roles.desc19": "Author only. Shown only when a task someone else completed is awaiting review.",
    "manual.roles.desc2": "Can edit everything: title · due date · owner · CCs · content. Changes are bundled into one update notification when the detail view is closed.",
    "manual.roles.desc20": "Owner · CCs — not the author.",
    "manual.roles.desc21": "For public tasks without an owner, anyone who can see them (except the author). Posts and polls can't be taken.",
    "manual.roles.desc22": `Anyone who can see the task. If the workspace is set to "Edit permission or higher", people with view-only access can't comment.`,
    "manual.roles.desc23": "Deleted tasks stay in the trash and can be **restored**.",
    "manual.roles.desc24": "The person who posted the notice. They handle edits and ending the posting (even admins don't edit other people's notices).",
    "manual.roles.desc25": "All employees or selected people. They record that they've read it with the **Confirm** button, and the author sees who hasn't read it via the confirmation status (n/m). Recipients can also use notes · to-dos · attachments.",
    "manual.roles.desc26": "The author isn't notified when recipients confirm — for an all-employee notice, notifications would pour in for every person.",
    "manual.roles.desc27": "If you set the **post time** in the future, the notice stays scheduled until then and notifies recipients when it goes up. Notices can't repeat.",
    "manual.roles.desc28": "The customer who left the inquiry (an external account not in the employee directory). Excluded when determining who's involved on our side.",
    "manual.roles.desc29": "Any employee who can view it can edit — otherwise, with no one involved, no one could reply. Only the owner completes it.",
    "manual.roles.desc3": "Can check it done themselves. If the author completes it, there's no review step and it's simply finished.",
    "manual.roles.desc30": "Set by **Take**. Whoever takes it first handles the reply.",
    "manual.roles.desc31": "A comment from an employee is the reply. The customer receives only reply notifications, not other task box notifications.",
    "manual.roles.desc4": "Can revert a task the owner completed, with a reason, **only while it's awaiting review**. The reason is left as a comment and the person who completed it is notified.",
    "manual.roles.desc5": "**Not included** in confirmation — there's no need to record that you read what you wrote.",
    "manual.roles.desc6": "Check the content, handle it, then check the completion circle (○). Once completed, it goes to the author as **Awaiting review**.",
    "manual.roles.desc7": 'Record "I read it" with the **Confirm** button. When the owner confirms, the author is notified. Changing the status to In progress also counts as confirming.',
    "manual.roles.desc8": "Can edit — due dates and content change as work goes on. Status · note · to-dos can also be edited right in the list.",
    "manual.roles.desc9": "Break a big task into to-dos (a checklist), and if needed, promote a to-do into its own task to assign to someone else.",
    "manual.roles.intro1": 'Every task has one sender (author), one person who handles it (owner), and people who need to stay informed (CCs). All three are "involved", so even a **private** task is visible to them within the same workspace. This tab covers who can press what; workspace settings can add further restrictions.',
    "manual.roles.lead1": "The person who created the task. They decide what needs doing by when, and review the result once it's done.",
    "manual.roles.lead2": 'The one person who actually does the work. Once assigned, they get notifications from the start time, and the task gathers under "My tasks".',
    "manual.roles.lead3": "People who don't do the work directly but need to know about it. There can be several, and they record that they've read it.",
    "manual.roles.lead4": "People looking at the same task may have different buttons. If a button isn't shown, you don't have permission (it's hidden entirely rather than shown locked).",
    "manual.roles.lead5": 'A notice is "something to announce", not "work to assign", so it has no owner. Its recipients are the people who need to read it.',
    "manual.roles.lead6": "Inquiries from merchants or the website are written by customers, not our employees, so the usual involvement rules don't apply as-is.",
    "manual.roles.subtitle1": "The task's owner",
    "manual.roles.subtitle2": "The person who receives and handles it",
    "manual.roles.subtitle3": "People who need to stay informed",
